Library version: master @ cd42b99 (also present in 5.0.1 Bugfix release)
Platform: Windows 10 64-bit
Compiler: MSVC 2019 64-bit

Files produced by the STEP exporter (id = "stp") cannot be read by the STEP (IFC) loader.

For example, [this file](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JC3/ModelSplit/assimp-master-cd42b99/specific_tests/force_specific_importer/models/scene.stp) was produced by assimp's STEP exporter. However, reading it with the IFC loader fails with the error:

    IFC: Unrecognized file schema: automotive_design

The importer should probably at least be able to read files produced by the exporter. I do not know if the issue originates in the exporter, or in the importer, but I suspect it is the importer because I received similar errors for non-assimp-generated files (see below).

---

[This test program](https://github.com/JC3/ModelSplit/tree/assimp-master-cd42b99/specific_tests/force_specific_importer) (Qt not required) can be used to demonstrate the issue (it forces the use of a specific importer to work around #3791). Essentially it loads the file like this:

```
        Assimp::Importer importer;
        Assimp::BaseImporter *loader;
        Assimp::DefaultIOSystem io;

        loader = importer.GetImporter("stp");
        bool readable = loader->CanRead(filename, &io, false);
        bool readableSig = loader->CanRead(filename, &io, true);
        const aiScene *scene = loader->ReadFile(&importer, filename, &io);

        printf("File: %s\n", filename.c_str());
        printf("  CanRead(checkSig=false): %s\n", readable ? "yes" : "no");
        printf("  CanRead(checkSig=true):  %s\n", readableSig ? "yes" : "no");
        printf("  ReadFile:                %s\n", scene ? "success" : loader->GetErrorText().c_str());
```

When the test program is run as (hopefully this is self-explanatory):

    force_specific_importer -x stp models/scene.stp

It outputs (hopefully this is also self-explanatory):

```
assimp version: 5.0.1 (master @ cd42b995)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Importer:
  mName:       Industry Foundation Classes (IFC) Importer
  mFileExtns:  ifc ifczip stp
  mAuthor:
  mMaintainer:
  mComments:
-----------------------------------------------------------------
File: models/scene.stp
  CanRead(checkSig=false): no
  CanRead(checkSig=true):  yes
  ReadFile:                IFC: Unrecognized file schema: automotive_design
-----------------------------------------------------------------
```

(The failure of `CanRead` with checkSig = false is a separate issue and is also discussed at #3791.)

---

As an aside, I was actually unable to find *any* STEP files that the IFC importer could load. I got every reference model from https://www.cax-if.org/cax/cax_stepLib.php, then just tried to import all of them as well as the aforementioned scene.stp and a zero-length file as well (that entire set of files can be found [here](https://github.com/JC3/ModelSplit/tree/assimp-master-cd42b99/specific_tests/force_specific_importer/models)), and every one of them produced a fairly similar error. 

